# Dragonhawk, Fate's Tempest: "until your next end step" is the next end step that has not begun. Dragonhawk enters on turn 1
# (a Bolt is exiled and not played: 2 damage at that end step, Bot2 18). In that same end step, once that has resolved, Bot1
# flickers it with Ephemerate: the second trigger exiles a second Bolt, and this turn's end step has already begun, so Bot1
# may play it until the end step of turn 3. Bot1 declines the rebound cast and casts that Bolt on turn 3 (it would be gone if
# the permission ended with turn 1's end step). That cast card is not still exiled at turn 3's end step, so no more damage:
# Bot2 ends at 20 - 2 - 3 = 15.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Dragonhawk, Fate's Tempest
Ephemerate
